every now and then i get a friend or  family member saying that they're  interested in  buying some type of a business so this  wouldn't be about starting a business  but there might be an existing business  maybe it's a a convenience store or  maybe it's some type of  healthcare practice whatever it might be  and they say hey i'm going to buy this  from the existing owner and i think it's  going to be a great business and they'll  they'll often say it generates this much  money and i only have to put this much  in and it feels risk-free  and  what i tend to tell them and i don't  want to be one of these naysayer people  i say possibly  but what you always have to think about  is why are they selling it and sometimes  there's a good reason why they're  selling it maybe they're retiring and  they don't have someone to pass the  business on to and they see in you  kind of the the person that they would  love to see running that business going  forward that could be a a very  legitimate thing but oftentimes there  might be a situation where they might be  pumping up some of the numbers uh they  might be showing you the business in the  busy season or in the on the busy day  and so i wouldn't take especially if  it's a small business that doesn't have  auditing that doesn't have  really strict accounting practices  i would observe the business for a very  long period of time and i would take  your own data as to whether the numbers  you're hearing about are real and i also  wouldn't discount how much effort and  work the existing owners putting into it  and what happens to the business if  they're no longer there and so if all of  that works out and if it really does  make sense then yeah you might be on to  something
 

